==Latin==
{{wikipedia|lang=la}}

===Etymology===
Found in Old English as a component of the place name {{m|ang|Tinanmūþe|t=Tynemouth}}. Possibly of {{der|la|cel|-}} origin, from {{der|la|cel-pro|*tīn|t=river}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*teh₂-|t=to flow}}.<ref>The Brittonic Language in the Old North" (PDF). Scottish Place Name Society.</ref> Compare the river {{m|la|Tinna}}.

[[File:Quiet River Tyne - geograph.org.uk - 205421.jpg|right|thumb|View of the river]]

===Proper noun===
{{la-proper noun|Tina<1>}}

# The river [[Tyne]] in [[England]]

====Declension====
{{la-ndecl|Tina<1>}}

===References===
